# Cloudflare Pages routing — the equivalent of the "rewrites" block in
# vercel.json, minus the API.
#
# Status 200 means REWRITE, not redirect: the URL in the address bar does not
# change, the file is just served from somewhere else. A 301/302 here would put
# ".html" back in front of the delegate, which is the thing these exist to
# remove.
#
# Pages serves a real file if one exists at the path before it consults this
# file, so "/admin/*" cannot swallow "/admin/assets/...". That is also why
# there is no explicit assets rule, unlike the Vercel regex which had to
# exclude them by hand.
#
# There is deliberately NO /api rule. Cloudflare Pages has no Express to route
# to; while the API stays on Vercel, the two front ends reach it by absolute
# URL through VITE_API_BASE_URL. See MIGRATION.md.

/register    /register.html      200
/admin       /admin/index.html   200
/admin/*     /admin/index.html   200
